The 2022–23 '''Saudi Pro League''' (known as the '''[[Roshn]] Saudi League''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 48th edition of the [[Saudi Pro League|top-tier Saudi football league]], established in [[1974–75 Saudi Categorization League|1974]], and the 15th edition since it was rebranded as the '''Saudi Pro League''' in [[2008–09 Saudi Pro League|2008]], Fixtures for the first half of the 2022–23 season were announced on 4 August 2022.<ref>{{cite web |title=إعلان مواعيد مباريات الدور الأول من الدوري السعودي |date=4 August 2022 |url=https://www.btolat.com/news/290790}}</ref>

[[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] were the three-time defending champions after winning their recording extending 18th title [[2020–21 Saudi Professional League|last season]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الهلال يُتّوج بلقب دوري المحترفين للمرة الثالثة على التوالي |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/viewstory.php?lang=ar&newsid=2366007}}</ref> [[Al-Adalah FC|Al-Adalah]], [[Khaleej FC|Al-Khaleej]], and [[Al Wehda FC|Al-Wehda]] join as the three promoted clubs from the [[2021–22 Saudi First Division League|2021–22 Yelo League]].<ref>{{cite web |title=السعودية: صعود الخليج والعدالة والوحدة إلى دوري الكبار |url=https://aawsat.com/home/article/3671656 }}{{Dead link|date=July 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> They replaced [[Al-Ahli Saudi FC|Al-Ahli]], [[Al-Faisaly FC|Al-Faisaly]], and [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]] who were relegated to the [[2022–23 Saudi First Division League|2022–23 Yelo League]]. The winner will play in the [[2023 FIFA Club World Cup]] in Saudi Arabia as the host club.

On 27 May, [[Al-Ittihad Club (Jeddah)|Al-Ittihad]] secured their ninth league title, with one game to spare, following a 3–0 away win against [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الاتحاد بطلاً لدوري روشن.. ويشارك في كأس العالم للأندية 2023 بالسعودية |url=https://www.okaz.com.sa/sport/saudi/2134452}}</ref> [[Al-Batin FC|Al-Batin]] were the first team to be relegated following a 1–0 defeat away to Al-Ittihad on 23 May.<ref>{{cite web |title=الباطن.. 2023.. الحصيلة الأسوأ |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/806694/}}</ref> [[Al-Adalah FC|Al-Adalah]] were the second and final club to be relegated following a 2–0 home defeat to [[Ettifaq FC|Al-Ettifaq]] on the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=بعد 367 يوما.. العدالة يعود إلى "يلو" |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/807521/}}</ref>

==Overview==
===Changes===
On 14 April 2022, the Saudi FF announced that the number of teams in the [[Saudi Professional League|Pro League]] 2023–24 season would be increased from 16 to 18 teams. To prepare for this change, only 2 teams would be relegated to the First Division League and 4 teams would be promoted to the Pro League.<ref name="alarabiya.net">{{cite web |title=رسمياً.. زيادة عدد أندية الدوري السعودي والأجانب |url=https://www.alarabiya.net/sport/saudi-sport/2022/04/14/%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%8B-%D8%B2%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A9-%D8%B9%D8%AF%D8%AF-%D8%A3%D9%86%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%AC%D8%A7%D9%86%D8%A8}}</ref>

===Name sponsorship===
On 23 August 2022, the Saudi Pro League (SPL) announced that they had signed a sponsorship deal with real estate company [[Roshn]]. As part of the sponsorship deal, the Saudi Pro League would be known as the Roshn Saudi League (RSL) for the next 5 seasons.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://spl.com.sa/en/node/4202|date=August 23, 2022|title=Saudi Pro League renamed to Roshn Saudi League|publisher=SPL|access-date=August 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220920170729/https://spl.com.sa/en/node/4202|archive-date=September 20, 2022|url-status=dead}}</ref>

